[Music]  hey everyone i'm lucy and i'm joined by  aaron flynn to talk a little bit about  nightingale so we saw a little bit of  the game awards we've seen some more at  uh summer game fest  aaron like what's the what's the  elevator pitch  uh so nightingale is a survival crafting  game set in the shared world gaslamp  fantasy universe where we've created  ourselves um and it brings a lot of  really interesting mechanics to survival  crafting and genre really like and the  thing we announced today was this thing  we call realm cards and so realm cards  let you as the player control portals  and because we have this complex  procedurally generated system to make  these realms and make these levels the  realm cards themselves influence and  control and help players have agency  over what they're going to see on the  other side of the portal so rather than  just a big vast open world  you go through these realms and these  realms are actually controlled and  manipulated by what you play in the  realm card system to open the portal and  go through so is there any kind of limit  on  how many realm cards i can play like  what what is the um  if i'm if i'm setting up  what am i what is it gonna look like yes  you're gonna get a few limitations there  so you get to play a variety of realm  cards you'll control your biome you'll  control um some of the major things  you'll see in the other side um you get  to control certain aspects of other  things like weather and stuff like that  and all that leads to changing the  experience and making the experience  exactly what you would want on the other  side and then in turn with that  different rewards and different  challenges or present themselves because  of what you've played  so how i mean how flexible is this  system then how often am i going to be  using the realm cards to change the  world that i'm playing  so every time you go through a portal  you're gonna get a chance to play round  cards um and the hope is that players  will find a lot of things to discover  and explore and  and have interest in in a realm and then  you know maybe after a few hours they  might decide to move on to the next  realm and see what's there for them  there might be quests to help you push  forward and things like that so that's  our hope we want to see players doing  that so lots to uncover in these realms  lots of mysteries lots to discover and  then you'll have a chance to earn more  realm cards and craft more of them and  then you'll go off to the next one try  something else so a lot of uh  customization a lot of like different  chances to try new things let's take a  look talk a little bit about kind of the  aesthetic you mentioned like gas lamp  why did you opt for that as a kind of  setting the aesthetic the tone yeah  great question so the gaslamp fantasy  idea came to us because originally we  wanted to do a fantasy game we knew that  much but some of us had made high  fantasy games like dragon age and things  like that but we decided that maybe a  contemporary fantasy setting was a  little better so something a little more  grounded in in what you recognize today  with certain outfits and certain um  certain weapons and gear and things like  that and so  in exploring that space we really like  this notion of the victorian era and  what it offered there so we got some of  the things to recognize you're going to  get typical shaped you know axes and  typical shaped knives like that at the  same time you have guns and things like  that but and we get really cool looking  cloaks and outfits and and helmets and  hats and everything and we just really  like that aesthetic and so from very  early in the project we embraced that  and embraced the architecture you get as  well you get all sorts of things that  you recognize as as being actual houses  or being actual um constructions  and we just fell in love with it early  in the early in the development was  there ever anything else on the table or  was it you know you kind of just saw  gaslight fans and you're like okay this  is it this is the kind of catch-all yeah  i think it was that actually i think we  didn't take very long before we after a  couple of concepts and a couple of ideas  going back and forth we just we just  said a lot so this is it we want this we  can bring this world to life  so you're gearing uh are you still  gearing for a 2022 release yeah that's  the plan um we're going to be having our  our play tests and closed alphas very  soon we want to get this trailer out now  we're gonna uh begin to prepare our  builds for that so stay tuned for more  on that front but uh yeah all all goes  well we'll be out in the next uh before  2022's over wow and so i  can i play solo or is this just you know  i can group up with a bunch of friends  kind of like valham style where you can  play by yourself but it really shines  when you're built yeah i think that's a  great way to say it you can definitely  play solo um you know it's not a game  for for particularly large groups so  it's not an mmorpg it's a game for small  groups friends  uh you know high trust relationships  where you'll know people and you bring  them in  invite them to your realm when they can  come explore around you can go to their  realm etc  and so that's really the sweet spot for  us this solo to small group play  so how many are you thinking about in  terms of small group like four we  haven't pinned it down yet but it should  be bigger than four a little bigger than  four i guess in terms of like you know  the original concept and we're gonna do  a bigger interview where we kind of  delve into this as well but it's like  where did where did the the seed of  nightingale kind of come from um so you  know the seed came from a few  conversations years and years ago um uh  our art director neil thompson and i had  both read a book called jonathan strange  and mr norrell by suzanna clarke she's  an english author and just fell in love  with it it was set in the napoleonic  wars and it was a story about the  rekindling of magic that came from the  fae and two wizards who had each  independently found magic again and had  each found different paths and fall  different paths to to harness it and use  it and we just loved that story we just  loved that um that concept and idea and  it kind of rolled around in the back of  niels and mai's mind for quite a while  and when we started inflection neil was  came along from from day one and we  started to bat the idea around there as  we thought about this game i thought  what if we had a setting like that and  so we take a lot of inspiration from  jonathan's strategy mr brown  well aaron is there anything else you  want to quickly say about nightingale  no this would be great thank you so much  i hope people enjoy and get to see a lot  more about what realm cards can do  because they're pretty flexible and it's  pretty awesome to watch players uh play  the game you can also play round cards  with your friends so you could play a  card and i could play card and then you  know we'll get to team up like that and  do things like that so it forms some  social gameplay as well which i really  like awesome thank you so much and for  more on nightingale make sure to stay  tuned to gamespot

